# Shemá — export and import (BE-14 · OBT-403)
#
# The export is a report that leaves, not a backup that returns. Four things to know before
# running anything below:
#   * the file is the caller's scope, and every row is reduced for everybody: a project in a
#     sensitive country leaves with its region where the place was, an empty base and
#     `locationWithheld: true` — the region's own coordinator included;
#   * the header says what the file holds, when and by whom it was made, over which scope, and
#     that it is confidential; how many places were withheld is told to coordination only;
#   * every file is recorded in `shema_exports` before it is handed back — `meta.exportId` (and
#     the CSV's "Registro deste arquivo" line) names the row;
#   * the import refuses the exported file. It takes a JSON list of `Project` records, checks all
#     of them before applying any, applies them as one write, and takes no authorization from
#     the file: `prayerVisibility`, the recording and a need's `prayerShared` are ignored.
#
# Before running: seed the app and its roles, grant one, and give the account a region.
#   uv run python scripts/seed_apps_roles.py
#   uv run python scripts/grant_app_role.py coord.local@test.com shema coordinator

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@accessToken = {{shema_login.response.body.tokens.access_token}}

### Login — named, so every request below reuses the token
# @name shema_login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "coord.local@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### The caller's projects as JSON — `{meta, projects}`
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/export/projects?format=json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### The same, as the spreadsheet: CSV with a BOM, `;`-separated, headed in English
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/export/projects?format=csv&lang=en
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Import one record — created if the caller's scope does not hold the id, updated if it does
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/import/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  {
    "id": "lingua-exemplo-vale-novo",
    "languageName": "Língua Exemplo",
    "bridgeLanguage": "Português",
    "team": "Base Exemplo",
    "objective": ["NT"],
    "location": "Vale Novo",
    "prayerRequests": "Arrives unauthorized, whatever the line below says.",
    "prayerVisibility": "rede"
  }
]
